== S7: yamale 6.1.0 day() semantics
class Day(Validator):
    """Day validator. Format: YYYY-MM-DD"""
    value_type = date
    tag = "day"
    constraints = [con.Min, con.Max]
    def _is_valid(self, value):
        return isinstance(value, date)
schema `review_by: day(max=2026-08-24)` (unquoted): SCHEMA SYNTAX ERROR
  ("leading zeros in decimal integer literals are not permitted"; the constraint
  argument is parsed as a Python expression and must be a quoted string)
schema `review_by: day(max="2026-08-24")`:
  good.yaml   (review_by 2026-08-01) -> Validation success, exit 0
  lapsed.yaml (review_by 2026-09-30) -> "2026-09-30 is greater than 2026-08-24", exit 1
grep for today/date.today/now() across yamale validators: no hits.
Conclusion: min/max are static literals baked into the schema text; no constraint
compares a value against the current date.

